FINDING — the device record carries its datasheet in the document and the page never draws it
  kg_demo.json, dev-hearing-aid-2019:
    "link": "https://example.org/datasheets/8ch-bte-hearing-aid"
  docs/DATA-CONTRACT.md (this PR) describes a device as "carries `link`, its datasheet, and `text`",
  and scripts/schema/kg-1-health.schema.json says the link is "the datasheet — the manufacturer's
  page or PDF describing what this thing is and what it forbids".
  On the page: 0 anchors with an http(s) href in the whole document (graph view opened and closed
  again to check), and the record panel above lists two actionable things — "open the document"
  (the audiology report PDF, the source) and "derived_from" (the same PDF). The datasheet URL is
  never rendered.
  Cause, read in the template this PR does not touch: `renderRecord()` in body/index.html builds
  the heading, the kind line, the text, WHERE IT CAME FROM (the `source` document and its link) and
  LINKED ITEMS, and prints no link of the record's own — its comment says so on purpose: "a record
  is not a lab report: it carries the document that holds it, never a lab's address". Analyses do
  render their own `link` (as a window.open button), so the omission is specific to records, and
  device is the first record kind whose whole point is a datasheet.
  body/index.html is not in this PR's diff (11 files: body/lib/state-list.js, case.html,
  docs/DATA-CONTRACT.md, index.html, kg_demo.json, scripts/case-artifact.test.ts,
  scripts/kg-contract.test.ts, scripts/lib/kg-contract.ts, scripts/schema/kg-1-health.schema.json,
  src/events.test.ts, src/events.ts), so no renderer change could have supplied it.
  The design artifact is silent on where a datasheet link belongs in the record panel, so the fix
  needs a layout decision as well as code — hence a fail, not a pass with a caveat.

SECOND FINDING — `bun run typecheck` fails on this head
  $ bun run typecheck
  src/events.ts(67,14): error TS2739: Type '{ observation: string[]; condition: string[];
  medication: string[]; procedure: string[]; encounter: string[]; document: string[]; }' is missing
  the following properties from type 'Record<"document" | "observation" | "condition" | "medication"
  | "procedure" | "encounter" | "immunization" | "device" | "allergy", readonly string[]'>:
  immunization, device, allergy
  This PR widened `EVENT_KINDS` (src/events.ts:17) and therefore `EventKind`, and left
  `REQUIRED_FIELDS: Record<EventKind, readonly string[]>` (src/events.ts:65) with the six old kinds.
  So the event model enforces no required field for an immunization, a device or an allergy, and the
  package does not compile. CI's verify job runs `review:gate` first and aborts on it, so the
  typecheck step has never run on this branch: "red only on the review gate" is not the whole
  picture — a passing verdict would turn verify red on typecheck in the same job.
  Everything else in the verify job is green on this head: lint 102 files, 1 pre-existing warning in
  scripts/e2e/policy.test.ts (not in the diff); test 964 pass / 0 fail; test:contract 25 fixtures,
  0 failures; check:case current at 300,921 bytes; check:demo current at 300,902 bytes; branch name
  feat/SCRUM-79_new-node-kinds valid. `bun run test` passing is itself the third observation: no
  unit test holds REQUIRED_FIELDS to EVENT_KINDS, which is how the missing three slipped through.

